// x86 target builtins that map directly to a Path64 intrinsic:
//   C2W_X86_BUILTIN(name after "__builtin_ia32_", intrinsic)
//
// Generated from GCC 4.2's builtin names (GCC/gcc/config/i386/i386.c:
// "__builtin_ia32_<name>" -> IX86_BUILTIN_<code>) joined with wgen's
// mapping (wgen/wgen_expr.cxx, WGEN_target_builtins: the cases that are
// only "*iopc = INTRN_<x>;"). Clang kept GCC's builtin names, so psclang
// gives each the same intrinsic wgen does. The builtins wgen expands by
// hand are in c2w_builtin.cxx (ConvertTargetBuiltinExpr).

C2W_X86_BUILTIN(addps, INTRN_ADDPS)
C2W_X86_BUILTIN(addsd, INTRN_ADDSD)
C2W_X86_BUILTIN(addss, INTRN_ADDSS)
